From e0c085fd85a0a26082811c935339839dd15c232a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Capture] A PQ capture carries the HDR metadata of the
 picture on the output

To map a PQ capture to SDR, swscale needs the peak of the picture: the
mastering display of its HDR metadata. CaptureResult has those fields
(hasDisplayMetadata, displayMetadata, hasLightMetadata, lightMetadata),
but the composite tap (screenshots) never filled them, and the video-only
tap (bookmark thumbnails) filled them with the video's own, which is not
the picture on the output where Hades makes one for it. Without them
swscale takes the whole range of PQ, 10000 cd/m2, as the peak, and
darkens the whole picture (issue #30).

CWinSystemBase::FillCaptureHdrMetadata() now says them where the window
system knows them:
- GBM: the metadata of the picture that SetHDR() was given and whose HDR
  signalling it left on the output: the video's own in passthrough, or
  that of the picture made for the output (HDR10 adapted to the display,
  Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10), as the picture's own, before what
  videoscreen.hadeshdr10limiton tells the display. None while no HDR is
  signalled.
- With native Dolby Vision (the capture reads the picture before it is
  packed): the source display of the RPU and its L6, or in Low-Latency
  the peak and black of the display that Hades maps the picture to.
Both taps fill them for a PQ capture through FillOutputHdrMetadata(); the
video-only tap keeps the video's own where the window system does not
know them. HLG is relative to its display and takes none.

Tests: TestCaptureMetadata (filled for PQ where known, left alone where
not, never for HLG or SDR).
